    "text": "Two things to look at. First, it's a compact blob with no strange structure, so the blur was matched with a smooth shape. Second, the numbers add up to about one. That sum is the flux scale between the two nights: near one means the brightness agreed. If the target were the sharper image, you would blur the target instead, never sharpen. For this pair, the reference is the sharper one.",
